I'm pissed.

Not just annoyed, but major-league pissed.

I was just killed on level 25 of the best game of Nethack 3 that I've ever
played.  Good enough to put me at #4 on the local high scores list.  But I'm
not pissed just because I was killed.  It's WHY I was killed.

I looked upon the Medusa.

WHY did I look upon the Medusa?

Because it wasn't represented by an '8'!

In the previous version of Nethack, the Medusa was an '8'.  When I saw a @,
I figured it was an Elf, or a Priest, or something like that.  But when I
teleported into the room (I hadn't yet found a ring of teleport control,
although I DID have rings of regeneration, polymorph, and polymorph control
and was having loads of fun as a vampire lord), I looked upon the Medusa and
instantly turned to stone.

Unfair?  Damn straight.  First of all, it would have been nice to know that
the Medusa was now represented by a '@'.  But second, I **HATE** instant
deaths.  At least with cockatrices, you get a turn or two to try to avert your
impending petrification.  The Medusa just outright stones you.

Unfair.

Sigh... On the brigher side, NEXT time I'll know.

